			<div class="content" id="post-content-4689281">
									

<p>Thank you for your time and feedback. I try to keep my definition consistent with the example laid out in Sheldon Katz's memo in SCP-4703. There, PeppersGhost mentions:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Generally we interpret and exercise the law through the scrutiny of semantics, reasoning, and precedent, yet bureaucratohazards such as SCP-4703 are not necessarily predicated on such things—in fact, the law as most know it has very little to do with the matter.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Anomalies, from my understanding, are defined as being inconsistent with baseline reality, the set of all universal principles considered 'normal'. Bureaucratohazards adjust baseline reality around themselves to include them- often, in ways that don't quite <em>mesh</em> correctly, which allows the Foundation to discover them.</p>

							</div>

								
					
